    "created_at": "2021-09-11T16:34:54Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-09-11T16:34:54Z",
    "body": "After having implemented this, I guess a far better feature request would be n format strings that could be swapped between with an argument.\r\n\r\nFor my case, in retrospect, maintaining two separate config files doesn't make a lot of sense.  I suspect that most users would want to keep the vast majority of their settings between switchable prompts, certainly that was the case for me.  A related issue, (which I should probably open a separate issue for) is having context-dependent \"boundary\" characters for different prompt elements, though that would be a change that certainly seems like a hell of a lot more work.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
